"Which is...?"

329
00:25:42,353 --> 00:25:45,953
「あまりにも無能すぎるがゆえに、
"Because you are so utterly incompetent..."

330
00:25:45,953 --> 00:25:48,353
君は探偵として勘定にも入れられていなかったのだ！」
"...you weren't even counted as a detective!"

331
00:25:48,353 --> 00:25:50,353
「ひどーい！」
"How cruel!"

332
00:25:51,453 --> 00:25:54,953
およしになって おやめになって 怪事件
Please stop, please don't do it, mysterious cases!

333
00:25:54,953 --> 00:25:58,353
お騒ぎ揺らす 探偵さん
Stirring up a commotion, Mr. Detective!

334
00:25:58,553 --> 00:26:01,353
ノックすれば ガチの目論見
If you knock, there lies a serious plot!

335
00:26:01,353 --> 00:26:02,853
行かないで
Please don't go!

336
00:26:02,853 --> 00:26:05,353
おおもう 先生のいじわる いけず
Oh dear, you're so mean and unkind, Sensei!

337
00:26:05,353 --> 00:26:08,353
列車トリック 発火トリック 難事件
Train tricks, ignition tricks, difficult cases!

338
00:26:08,353 --> 00:26:12,353
推理作家の先生！
Mystery writer Sensei!

339
00:26:12,353 --> 00:26:15,353
うだらはだらうだらはだら言わないで ああもう
Don't say such nonsense, oh geez!

340
00:26:15,853 --> 00:26:19,353
頭がこんがらがってきたけれど
My head is getting all tangled up, but...

341
00:26:19,353 --> 00:26:23,353
かわいやかわいや トリック暴いて
How cute, how cute, expose the trick...

342
00:26:23,353 --> 00:26:25,853
通りゃんせ
...and pass through!

343
00:26:40,353 --> 00:26:43,353
小さい2人の子供が約束した、
Two small children made a promise...

344
00:26:43,353 --> 00:26:47,353
ずっといっしょに笑っていようの約束。
...a promise to always laugh together.

345
00:26:47,853 --> 00:26:52,353
今もなお、2人の絆は確かなもので…
Even now, their bond remains certain...

346
00:26:52,353 --> 00:26:56,853
…友情と愛情が織りなす素敵な物語。
...a wonderful story woven of friendship and love.

347
00:26:57,353 --> 00:27:04,353
あははっ…なんでもないことに、妙にツボっちゃう時あるよねっ
Ahaha... sometimes we burst out laughing at the most trivial things, right?

348
00:27:15,353 --> 00:27:19,353
あー恋に落ちたまゆら 開花止まらないや
Ah, falling in love for a fleeting moment, the blooming won't stop

349
00:27:19,353 --> 00:27:22,853
何度も捲って 心をかし
Turning the pages over and over, my heart is charmed

350
00:27:22,853 --> 00:27:26,853
泣いてばっかだったの それがどうだ今や
I used to do nothing but cry, but look at me now

351
00:27:26,853 --> 00:27:29,853
腹よじるくらい笑う
Laughing so hard my stomach twists

352
00:27:29,853 --> 00:27:33,853
ずっと一緒に笑う
Always laughing together

353
00:27:34,353 --> 00:27:38,353
きみが持ってる白い花に
To the white flower that you hold,

354
00:27:38,353 --> 00:27:41,353
あたし見合わないな 悲しくなる
I don't seem to suit it, and it makes me sad

355
00:27:41,353 --> 00:27:45,153
無垢な恋とか正しさとか
About pure love or what is right,

356
00:27:45,153 --> 00:27:48,853
誰も教えてくれなかった
no one ever taught me

357
00:27:49,353 --> 00:27:52,853
昨日会ったばっかで
We only just met yesterday,

358
00:27:52,853 --> 00:27:56,353
今日もどっか会えたらなんて思う暮らし 慎ましくないよね
yet wishing we'd meet again today isn't very modest, is it?

359
00:27:56,353 --> 00:27:59,853
全部許されたの びっくりしちゃってさ
Everything was forgiven, it completely surprised me

360
00:27:59,853 --> 00:28:02,853
涙あふれてたよ
and my tears overflowed

361
00:28:03,853 --> 00:28:07,853
もう愛になる花歌 透き通った空に
A humming song that has turned into love under the transparent sky

362
00:28:07,853 --> 00:28:11,853
手を繋いでった 夢のしるし
We held hands, a sign of our dream

363
00:28:11,853 --> 00:28:15,353
どんな前世だってさ 忘れたっていいんだ
No matter what our past lives were, it's fine to forget them

364
00:28:15,353 --> 00:28:19,353
きみと笑えるなら
as long as I can laugh with you

365
00:28:19,353 --> 00:28:22,853
心が触れるたび綺麗な音鳴る
Every time our hearts touch, a beautiful sound rings out

366
00:28:22,853 --> 00:28:26,353
目と目が合ってくすぐったいね
Our eyes meet, and it's ticklish

367
00:28:26,353 --> 00:28:30,353
なんでもないこと妙にツボるね
We burst out laughing at the most trivial things

368
00:28:30,353 --> 00:28:34,353
全部教えてくれてありがとう
Thank you for teaching me everything

369
00:28:49,353 --> 00:28:52,853
きみが持ってる白い花を
The white flower that you hold,

370
00:28:52,853 --> 00:28:56,353
あたしの紅色と合わせたら
if I combine it with my crimson red...

371
00:28:56,353 --> 00:29:00,353
霜が溶けては雲が行く
The frost melts and the clouds drift away

372
00:29:00,353 --> 00:29:04,353
もう寒くないよ
I'm not cold anymore

373
00:29:08,853 --> 00:29:12,853
あー恋に落ちたまゆら 開花止まらないや
Ah, falling in love for a fleeting moment, the blooming won't stop

374
00:29:12,853 --> 00:29:16,353
何度も捲って 心をかし
Turning the pages over and over, my heart is charmed

375
00:29:16,353 --> 00:29:19,853
泣いてばっかだったの それがどうだ今や
I used to do nothing but cry, but look at me now

376
00:29:19,853 --> 00:29:23,353
腹よじるくらい笑う
Laughing so hard my stomach twists

377
00:29:23,353 --> 00:29:27,853
ずっと一緒に笑って
Laughing together forever...

378
00:29:27,853 --> 00:29:31,153
(恋に落ちたまゆら)
(falling in love for a fleeting moment)

379
00:29:31,153 --> 00:29:34,853
心をかし
my heart is charmed

380
00:29:34,853 --> 00:29:37,353
(愛になる花歌)
(a humming song turning into love)

381
00:29:37,353 --> 00:29:40,853
ずっと一緒に笑う
always laughing together

382
00:29:40,853 --> 00:29:46,353
最後の日を笑う
laughing on our final day

383
00:29:54,353 --> 00:30:00,353
これは、遠い遠い名も知らぬ世界で、
This is a story in a far, far away, nameless world...

384
00:30:01,641 --> 00:30:06,741
死の呪いがかけられた 少女のお話
This is the story of a girl cursed with death.

385
00:30:25,641 --> 00:30:31,841
遠い遠い時の果て そこに住まう人は皆
At the end of a time far, far away, everyone who lived there...

386
00:30:31,841 --> 00:30:38,141
皆永遠の命をもつ 世界での話
...possessed eternal life in that world's tale.

387
00:30:38,141 --> 00:30:44,641
赤い実の成る木の下 生まれながらに
Under the tree bearing red fruit, from the moment she was born...

388
00:30:44,641 --> 00:30:51,441
死の呪いがかけられた 少女の話
...this is the story of a girl cursed with death.

389
00:31:00,641 --> 00:31:04,641
色付いた街外れ 蒼く光る湖畔
On the colorful outskirts of town, by the blue glowing lakeshore...

390
00:31:04,641 --> 00:31:08,641
赤い実のお菓子屋
...stands a sweet shop of red fruit.

391
00:31:08,641 --> 00:31:13,641
ちょっぴり寒くなった今日は 妙に誇らしげ
Today, as it grew a bit colder, she felt strangely proud...

392
00:31:13,641 --> 00:31:17,141
自信作を売りに行く
...and went to sell her masterpiece.

393
00:31:17,141 --> 00:31:23,141
待ってて 今度こそ 美味しいんだから
Just wait, it's definitely delicious this time!

394
00:31:25,641 --> 00:31:32,141
時計塔の見える市 驚いた 珍しく賑やかね
At the market by the clock tower, she was surprised to see it so lively.

395
00:31:32,641 --> 00:31:34,841
La La Lu La Lucky!!

396
00:31:34,841 --> 00:31:37,641
物憂げな街の隅 ひとり
Alone in a gloomy corner of the town...

397
00:31:37,641 --> 00:31:42,641
赤い実のパイ どうですか 自信作なの
"Would you like a red fruit pie? It's my masterpiece."

398
00:31:42,641 --> 00:31:45,141
さんぽのびともひとつも売れやせず
Not a single passerby bought one.

399
00:31:45,641 --> 00:31:49,641
少女を見て蔑む人達
People looked at the girl with disdain.

400
00:31:49,641 --> 00:31:53,641
みんなと何も変わらないのに
Even though she is no different from anyone else.

401
00:31:53,641 --> 00:31:56,941
美味しくできたのに
Even though she made it so delicious.

402
00:31:56,941 --> 00:32:01,141
今日も声は届かないのね
Today, too, her voice won't reach anyone.

403
00:32:01,141 --> 00:32:05,641
まるで透明になったみたいだわ
It's as if she has become invisible.

404
00:32:05,641 --> 00:32:09,641
そうして誰もが知らぬ振りをした
And so, everyone pretended not to notice.

405
00:32:09,641 --> 00:32:14,141
何故なら少女は呪われているから
Because the girl is cursed.

406
00:32:14,641 --> 00:32:21,641
死んた世界で唯ひとり生きていた少女の話
This is the story of a girl who lived all alone in a dead world.

407
00:32:30,641 --> 00:32:34,641
夜なべでアレンジパイとにっこりスマイル引っ提げ
Working through the night, with an improved pie and a bright smile...

408
00:32:34,641 --> 00:32:38,141
少女はまだ諦めない
...the girl still hasn't given up.

409
00:32:38,641 --> 00:32:43,141
時計塔の針も空を指してお腹も鳴るそんな時
As the clock tower's hand pointed to the sky and her stomach rumbled...

410
00:32:44,641 --> 00:32:48,641
ふと後ろから人が少女を押す
...suddenly, someone pushed her from behind.

411
00:32:48,641 --> 00:32:53,141
甘いカゴは落ちる
The sweet basket fell.

412
00:32:53,641 --> 00:32:59,141
お菓子を踏み行く人達 平気な顔をしてさ
People trampled the treats, completely unbothered.

413
00:32:59,141 --> 00:33:01,841
惨めに拾い集める
As she miserably gathered them up...

414
00:33:01,841 --> 00:33:06,141
ふともうひとりの手が
...suddenly, another hand appeared.

415
00:33:06,641 --> 00:33:14,141
どろどろのパイを徐に口に入れて「美味しいね」
He slowly put the muddy pie into his mouth and said, "It's delicious."

416
00:33:14,641 --> 00:33:18,641
その声で色は溢れた
With those words, color overflowed.

417
00:33:18,641 --> 00:33:22,641
まるで輪郭を描いたみたいだわ
It's as if outlines were finally drawn.

418
00:33:22,641 --> 00:33:27,141
そうして彼は手を差し出した
And so, he reached out his hand to her.

419
00:33:27,141 --> 00:33:31,141
何故なら少女に呪われて...
Because even if he is cursed by the girl...

420
00:33:31,141 --> 00:33:41,141
死んだ世界で唯ふたり生きていた遠い物語
This is the distant tale of two people who lived alone in a dead world.

421
00:33:51,641 --> 00:33:58,141
街の人達は哀れむ 赤い実を食べて呪われた者を
The townsfolk pitied those cursed by eating the red fruit.

422
00:33:58,141 --> 00:34:02,141
永遠に生きられずに死ぬのか
"Will they die without being able to live forever?"

423
00:34:02,141 --> 00:34:08,141
嗚呼 なんて可哀想な話
"Ah, what a tragic story..."

424
00:34:08,641 --> 00:34:14,641
ふたりは笑う それでも笑う
The two of them laughed, and still, they laughed.

425
00:34:14,641 --> 00:34:21,141
La La La とっても素敵な呪いね
La La La, what a truly wonderful curse.

426
00:34:21,141 --> 00:34:31,141
例え明日死んでも 『今』が確かで大切になるから
Even if we die tomorrow, "now" becomes real and precious to us.

427
00:34:35,641 --> 00:34:39,141
もう声は届かないのね
Her voice won't reach anyone anymore.

428
00:34:39,141 --> 00:34:43,641
まるで透明になったみたいだわ
It's as if she has become invisible.

429
00:34:43,641 --> 00:34:48,141
そうして誰もが知らぬ振りをした
And so, everyone pretended not to notice.

430
00:34:48,141 --> 00:34:53,141
何故なら世界が呪われているから
Because the world itself is cursed.

431
00:34:54,141 --> 00:34:58,141
『永遠』の呪いは解かれていた
The curse of "eternity" had been broken.

432
00:34:58,141 --> 00:35:01,641
まるでふたりの方が狂ったみたいだろう
It's almost as if the two of them were the ones who went mad.

433
00:35:02,722 --> 00:35:06,822
そしていつか笑うように眠る
And then, sleep someday as if smiling...

434
00:35:06,822 --> 00:35:11,222
何故ならふたりは放たれているから
Because the two of us have been set free.

435
00:35:11,222 --> 00:35:19,122
死んだ世界でただふたりだけが幸せだった
In this dead world, only we two were happy.

436
00:36:12,322 --> 00:36:16,522
さて、今日はこれくらいにしておきましょう。
Well, let's call it a day here.

437
00:36:17,122 --> 00:36:20,522
…そろそろ時間になりましたし
...Since it's about that time anyway.

438
00:36:20,722 --> 00:36:23,722
…え？ どこへ向かうのかって？
...Eh? Where are we going, you ask?

439
00:36:24,522 --> 00:36:28,222
今日は何の日かご存知ないのですか？
Don't you know what day it is today?

440
00:36:29,222 --> 00:36:35,722
今日は、この王国の地下深くにある冥界でのハロウィンパーティーですよ！
Today is the Halloween party in the underworld, deep beneath this kingdom!

441
00:36:35,922 --> 00:36:40,222
死者と生者が楽しむ年に一度のお祭りです。
It's a once-a-year festival for the dead and the living to enjoy together.

442
00:36:40,522 --> 00:36:43,222
さぁ、一緒に向かいましょう。
Come, let's head there together.

443
00:36:44,222 --> 00:36:46,022
でも、気を付けて。
But please, be careful.

444
00:36:46,022 --> 00:36:50,122
パーティーとは言え、死者が住まう冥界です。
Even if it's a party, it is the underworld where the dead reside.

445
00:36:50,322 --> 00:36:55,722
誰かの思念や死者達によって奇妙な事が起こるかもしれません。
Strange things might happen due to someone's lingering thoughts or the dead.

446
00:36:55,922 --> 00:37:00,522
でも、決してそちらに耳を傾けすぎてはいけませんよ…
But you must never pay too much attention to them...

447
00:37:00,722 --> 00:37:04,222
それでは、参りましょう。
Well then, let us go.

448
00:37:11,722 --> 00:37:16,722
蒼炎
[Title: Blue Flame]

449
00:37:50,222 --> 00:37:53,722
誰かが言いました
Someone once said...

450
00:37:53,722 --> 00:37:57,722
激しく燃えるものほど
...that the more intensely something burns...

451
00:37:57,722 --> 00:38:00,922
煌めく引き換えに
...in exchange for its brilliant sparkle...

452
00:38:00,922 --> 00:38:04,722
その身をすぐ焦がしきると
...the sooner it completely consumes itself.

453
00:38:12,922 --> 00:38:16,222
数ある燭台に
Upon the countless candlesticks...

454
00:38:16,222 --> 00:38:20,222
お好きな火を灯しましょう
...let's light your flame of choice.

455
00:38:20,222 --> 00:38:23,922
期待と裏腹に
Contrary to expectations...

456
00:38:23,922 --> 00:38:27,522
燻ればお生憎様
...if it only smolders, how unfortunate.

457
00:38:27,522 --> 00:38:31,522
ランランランラン 右手には錆びた時計
Lan, lan, lan, lan, a rusted watch in my right hand...

458
00:38:31,522 --> 00:38:35,522
ランランランラン 左には油の筒
...lan, lan, lan, lan, a tube of oil in my left.

459
00:38:35,522 --> 00:38:42,722
蝋のドレスを着飾って さあ固定
Now, dress up in a gown of wax.

460
00:38:42,722 --> 00:38:46,722
激しく 儚く
Violently, fleetingly...

461
00:38:46,722 --> 00:38:50,722
蒼く燃ゆる花びら
...petals burning in a blue flame.

462
00:38:50,722 --> 00:38:54,322
瞬き ゆらめく
Flickering and wavering...

463
00:38:54,322 --> 00:38:58,222
生を彩り照らせ
...color and light up this life...

464
00:38:58,222 --> 00:39:05,722
いずれ尽き果てる未来へと
...toward a future destined to eventually exhaust itself.

465
00:39:09,722 --> 00:39:12,722
揺り籠の目の前で
Right in front of the cradle...

466
00:39:12,722 --> 00:39:17,022
遍く飛び交う銃弾
...bullets fly far and wide.

467
00:39:17,022 --> 00:39:20,222
指だけ動かせば
With just a flick of a finger...

468
00:39:20,222 --> 00:39:24,222
容易くその火は潰える
...that flame is easily extinguished.

469
00:39:39,722 --> 00:39:46,722
仮初の情熱で 焼け爛れた舌では
With a tongue blistered by transient passion...

470
00:39:46,722 --> 00:39:54,722
上手く喋ることが できないようで
...it seems I cannot speak very well.

471
00:39:54,722 --> 00:40:01,722
喉元過ぎても 毒を孕ませて
Harbouring poison even if the danger passes...

472
00:40:01,722 --> 00:40:02,722
やがては
...eventually...

473
00:40:03,277 --> 00:40:10,077
やがては肺を腐らせるでしょう
Eventually, it will rot your lungs.

474
00:40:10,877 --> 00:40:13,877
揺らぐ死と生の狭間
Swaying in the threshold between life and death,

475
00:40:13,877 --> 00:40:17,877
焼ける心と歌う
I sing with a burning heart.

476
00:40:17,877 --> 00:40:24,177
描いた最愛の終幕を
The beloved finale I envisioned.

477
00:40:26,177 --> 00:40:33,477
激しく 儚く 蒼く燃ゆる花びら
Violently, fleetingly, the blue burning petals...

478
00:40:33,477 --> 00:40:41,477
瞬き ゆらめく 生を彩り照らせ
Flickering and swaying, coloring and illuminating life,

479
00:40:41,477 --> 00:40:48,677
いずれ尽き果てるその先へ
Towards the future that will eventually exhaust itself.

480
00:41:05,677 --> 00:41:11,177
あちらの世界に引きずり込まれないうちに 早く会場へ向かわないといけませんね。
Before we get dragged into that world, we must head to the venue quickly.

481
00:41:11,677 --> 00:41:14,177
気を付けてついてきてくださいね、
Please be careful and follow me.

482
00:41:14,177 --> 00:41:17,677
あまり深入りすると、おっと…
If you delve too deep, oops...

483
00:41:18,177 --> 00:41:22,677
そうそう、知らないほうがきっと懸命ですよ。
That's right, it's definitely wiser not to know.

484
00:41:22,677 --> 00:41:27,677
なんだかすっごく心地が良いよね。
Somehow, it feels incredibly comfortable, doesn't it?

485
00:41:39,677 --> 00:41:43,677
アメイジングハッピーハロウィンナイト
[Title: Amazing Happy Halloween Night]

486
00:41:44,177 --> 00:41:48,677
気づけば見知らぬ世界に立っていた
Before I knew it, I was standing in an unfamiliar world.

487
00:41:49,177 --> 00:41:55,177
何処かも分からず毎日毎日毎日泣いていた
Not knowing where I was, day after day after day, I was crying.

488
00:41:55,177 --> 00:41:56,477
なんて暇も無く
I didn't even have time to do that!

489
00:41:56,477 --> 00:41:58,877
Happy Time! おかしな面々が
Happy Time! Odd characters...

490
00:41:58,877 --> 00:42:01,177
Happy Time! おどけて転がるの
Happy Time! Fool around and tumble.

491
00:42:01,177 --> 00:42:03,877
Happy Time! その馬鹿馬鹿しさに
Happy Time! With all that silliness,

492
00:42:03,877 --> 00:42:06,177
希望も恐怖もなくなった
both hope and fear disappeared.

493
00:42:06,177 --> 00:42:09,677
確かそうアタシには
I'm pretty sure I had...

494
00:42:09,677 --> 00:42:13,677
為すべき仕事 愛の棲家
...a job to do, and a loving home.

495
00:42:13,677 --> 00:42:17,477
パンプキン ヘッドギア
Pumpkins, headgear...

496
00:42:17,477 --> 00:42:21,677
だけどなんかどーでもいい
But somehow, none of it matters.

497
00:42:22,677 --> 00:42:25,677
さぁ始まった夢の夜だ
Now it has begun, the night of dreams!

498
00:42:25,677 --> 00:42:27,977
音楽が響いて鳴り止まない
The music echoes and won't stop playing.

499
